# T5a step 6: the joiner half of "stop, author while absent, restart,
# converge" (design_docs/2026-07-28_turnstone_place_port_plan.md, "T5a",
# Scope). Runs as a SECOND process against the SAME appdata/root/profile the
# phase-1 joiner used (scenarios/place_joiner.scn), so the place binding,
# rendezvous and stores the worker persisted are retained offline at startup.
# Paired with the founder's phase-2 continuation in scenarios/place_founder.scn
# through the shared ${EXCHANGE} directory and ${FOUNDER_DIR} (the founder's
# capture dir, passed by scenarios/place_two_windows.ps1).
settle 30
key escape

# Retained history is visible immediately at startup, before any reconnect:
# the worker persisted place.json/place-rendezvous.json/place/ under
# TURNSTONE_ROOT and current_session points at it, so this is an offline
# reopen, not a fresh join.
wait-status 600 Retained history: 0 shared nodes, 2 messages

# A "Reconnect place" issued right after a live open in the SAME process is
# refused (store still locked); this IS the real restart that makes it valid.
act Reconnect place
settle 5
wait-status 600 Local rendezvous

# Wait for the founder's absent-authored message (written while this joiner
# was stopped) before expecting it to have converged.
wait-file 6000 ${FOUNDER_DIR}\founder_absent_authored.json
wait-status 3000 Retained history: 0 shared nodes, 3 messages

act Send place message
settle 5
type back again
key enter
settle 10
wait-status 600 Retained history: 0 shared nodes, 4 messages

# Signal the founder that the return leg is complete.
touch ${EXCHANGE}\joiner.returned

act Place status
settle 10
capture joiner_return
record-place joiner_return

log joiner return path complete
